    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Jedi_Academy_Training_Manual\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual\">Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual</a></i> </p><p><i>See also: <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Lightsaber_Construction\" title=\"Lightsaber Construction\">Lightsaber Construction</a></i> </p><p>A Trapped Grip requires the wielder to perform some <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Free_Action\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Free Action\">Free Action</a> (Usually pressing down on a hidden sensor, twisting a nondescript knob, or some other mundane task) before activating the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Lightsaber\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Lightsaber\">Lightsaber</a> safely. If the wielder does not perform this task at the time the weapon activates, the wielder takes 1d6 points of Energy damage, and again at the start of his or her turn until the trap is deactivated. Deactivating the trap is a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Free_Action\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Free Action\">Free Action</a> that is performed as a part of activating the weapon, and a DC 20 <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Perception\" title=\"Perception\">Perception</a> check can reveal the trap mechanism and the disarming action. </p>",
